# Security-critical file — this is what keeps secrets and the encrypted
# database out of published images. Getting .env or data/ into an image is
# a genuine credential/data leak (docker history / any pull of the image
# exposes every layer), not just repo hygiene. Verify after every change
# here by inspecting a built image's filesystem, not by re-reading this
# file — see README.md "Docker / deploy" for the check.

# Secrets — never build these into an image. Real deploy secrets are
# injected at runtime via `env_file` / orchestrator secrets, not baked in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# App data — the SQLCipher-encrypted DB (and any dev/plaintext DB) belongs
# on the mounted volume, never in an image layer.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# Host-built artifacts — node_modules is compiled for Windows on this
# machine and is useless (or actively broken, for the native module) inside
# the Linux image; .next is rebuilt fresh in the `build` stage.
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist

# VCS / agent tooling — not part of the shipped app.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.cache
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Editor / OS cruft.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Logs / debug.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Test artifacts / coverage / typecheck cache — not needed to build or run.
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Docs not needed inside the image (kept in the repo, not the build context).
README.md
